{#- Managed by ansible (role: dev_worker, ADR 0020). consul-template markup consumed by the bao
    agent, NOT by ansible: the agent renders each user's ~/.git-credentials from the KV path, so
    rotating the PAT in OpenBao reaches every worker without a playbook run. Everything outside
    the {{ }} actions is copied verbatim into the credential file, which is why this file carries no
    comment of its own — a Jinja comment emits nothing. The KV-v2 read path needs the `data/`
    segment (af/data/dev-workers/common, not af/dev-workers/common) and the value sits under
    .Data.data. The document and the login come from dev_worker_gitea_identity_cutover (defaults):
    common + dev-worker-bot, or this slot's own document + <slot>-bot — always switched together.
    Both are substituted unescaped into a quoted consul-template string and a URL. That is safe by
    validation, not by escaping: tasks/main.yml asserts them against ^(common|dev-worker-[0-9]+)$ and
    ^dev-worker(-[0-9]+)?-bot$ on every run, before anything renders this file. -#}
{% raw %}{{ with secret "af/data/dev-workers/{% endraw %}{{ dev_worker_gitea_cred_name }}{% raw %}" }}https://{% endraw %}{{ dev_worker_gitea_user }}{% raw %}:{{ .Data.data.gitea_pat }}@git.chifor.me{{ end }}{% endraw %}
